  "user": "Please look up transaction TX-0401 in my account records and verify its amount. Then explain which reason codes could apply; I have not yet told you what happened.",
  "answer": "I found TX-0401 in account ACC-1005 (EUR). The amount is **EUR 240.00**, a card payment to **TechMart Online** on 2026-07-20, status settled.\n\nFor context, your account also shows a second card payment to TechMart Online for **EUR 240.00** on 2026-07-14 (TX-0402), also settled. I'm pointing this out only because the amounts and merchant match. I haven't assumed anything about what happened.\n\nBased on the reason codes available for disputes, these could apply, depending on what happened:\n\n- **duplicate_charge**: You were charged more than once for the same purchase. This would fit if you bought one item and were billed both on 2026-07-14 and 2026-07-20.\n- **unauthorized_debit**: You did not authorise this payment.\n- **fraud_card_not_present**: The payment was made online without your card being present, and you did not make or approve it.\n- **goods_not_received**: You paid for something and it was never delivered.\n- **service_not_rendered**: You paid for a service that was not provided.\n\nTell me which situation matches, and I'll check whether a dispute can be opened under that code before doing anything. I won't open one without your confirmation.",
